<section image-layout="blank" id="sK9WZy6RzN"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="JI3xSAeLQU" vertical-align="start" colspan="44"><h2>A life redirected by obligation</h2><p font-size="18pt">The plot advances through choices made under increasing pressure—not through passive misfortune alone.</p><table col-widths="[16,22,22]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="--table-cell-padding:3pt 12pt"><tbody><tr><td background-color="accent"><p>Stage</p></td><td background-color="accent"><p>Choice under pressure</p></td><td background-color="accent"><p>Consequence carried forward</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Vow</b></p></td><td background-color="surface"><p>Kiều commits to Kim Trọng.</p></td><td><p>A shared future is imagined.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Family crisis</b></p></td><td background-color="surface"><p>She sells herself to rescue her family.</p></td><td><p>Filial duty redirects her life.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Exploitation</b></p></td><td background-color="surface"><p>She resists sale, coercion, and persecution.</p></td><td><p>Private vows meet a predatory market.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Brief reversal</b></p></td><td background-color="surface"><p>She acts beside Từ Hải.</p></td><td><p>Power opens, then closes through deception.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Return</b></p></td><td background-color="surface"><p>Giác Duyên’s rescue enables reunion.</p></td><td><p>Survival continues; harm is not erased.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p font-size="12pt">Condensed plot route; role labels are prioritized over a larger cast list.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="CtAdrnITem" padding="0" colspan="16"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/kMCAEh8py1gTY-civJCL-.png" saved-media-id="17vwjme5si9118s" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="vietnamese-manuscript-editorial" alt="Ink-and-opaque-pigment editorial illustration on warm dó-paper-like fibers, a non-documentary literary figure crossing successive Vietnamese gates toward a distant river, the path narrowing through shadow and opening again at dawn, lampblack, vermilion, old gold and indigo, manuscript and woodblock conventions, no text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>